  imagine module: test suite
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  [PASS] Color construction clamps, rounds, and reads every hex and named form
  [PASS] Color.parse() accepts every documented spelling and rejects the rest
  [PASS] bad colours raise rather than being silently accepted
  [PASS] Color conversions, luminance and contrast agree with the colors module
  [PASS] Color mixing, compositing and adjustment behave as documented
  [PASS] Image construction validates its dimensions and starts transparent
  [PASS] pixel reads and writes blend, replace and ignore out-of-range coordinates
  [PASS] a clipping rectangle confines drawing and can be cleared
  [PASS] the scanline rasterizer fills rectangles, ellipses and both winding rules
  [PASS] anti-aliasing can be turned off and produces partial coverage when on
  [PASS] stroke thickness is centred on the path
  [PASS] drawing onto a fully transparent image writes valid partial coverage
  [PASS] line caps can be butt, round or square, and only affect open ends
  [PASS] flood fill spreads four-connected and respects a barrier
  [PASS] linear and radial gradients interpolate, blend and stay inside their bounds
  [PASS] the resizing family produces the documented sizes and never mutates
  [PASS] cropping, padding, rotation and transposition report the right dimensions
  [PASS] mirroring and quarter turns move pixels in the documented direction
  [PASS] trim() removes a uniform border and degrades sensibly
  [PASS] lookup-table and colour-matrix filters produce the documented results
  [PASS] the lookup-table and matrix primitives validate their inputs
  [PASS] colour matrices combine correctly
  [PASS] convolution handles alpha correctly and finds real edges
  [PASS] the Gaussian blur spreads colour and validates its radius
  [PASS] pixelate() averages each block independently
  [PASS] compositing clips, honours opacity and applies blend modes
  [PASS] an image can be composited onto itself
  [PASS] place() positions by anchor and validates it
  [PASS] mask() takes alpha from another image and checks its size
  [PASS] histograms, auto levels, averages and dominant colours read the image correctly
  [PASS] every self-describing format round-trips at the right size
  [PASS] lossless formats preserve colour exactly and JPEG approximately
  [PASS] format names, extensions and media types resolve both ways
  [PASS] probing and capability reporting are honest about what this build can do
  [PASS] unsupported and malformed input raises instead of failing quietly
  [PASS] the WBMP codec round-trips, including multi-byte dimensions
  [PASS] images encode as data URLs
  [PASS] animations build, transform and round-trip through GIF
  [PASS] text measurement and rendering behave correctly (when a system font is available)
  [PASS] the built-in stroke font measures, scales, wraps and draws without any font file

